My favourite extension to hack (which I have been hacking in since
1.0.2) is random, magic-sounding scroll names a la rogue.  I sent it
off to the d-team; they didn't like it.  Hence I offer it to the
general public on an as-is basis.  You may hate it, you may love it.
You will have to support it.  If enough of you love it, maybe they
will change their mind.

Makes code a bit smaller (less static string space), save files bigger
and incompatable.  It is selected from config.h. 

This generates names like:
	skades			ashthefeg fezbaa	pash pelpp pash
	e'awokthe limanda	jatjen			lem retpiz apkaj
	quesel jen ap		kaj haqkre		oli desul
	uruinopef depp		kra ska			quaapef
	tospstrapil		debaa			quexor
	bli tro n'a		tha chi aampp		anikra

Has been tested quite thoroughly on hack 1.02 -> 3.0pl9, on Sun3s and
Sun4s. I don't have amiga/mac/pc access, so this may not work in those
environments. 

Apply this to 3.0pl9 source.
